  "exercises": [
    {
      "number": "1052",
      "source_number": "1052",
      "text": "1052. 用 $p$ 和 $q$ 表示方程 $x^2+px+q=0$ 的根的平方和。",
      "figure_refs": [],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1052",
          "source_excerpt": "用 $p$ 和 $q$ 表示方程 $x^2+px+q=0$ 的根的平方和。",
          "domain": "For the real-root reading, p,q are real and p^2-4q>=0. The identity also holds for complex p,q and complex roots.",
          "derivation": [
            "Vieta gives x1+x2=-p and x1*x2=q, counting multiplicity.",
            "x1^2+x2^2=(x1+x2)^2-2*x1*x2=p^2-2q."
          ],
          "all_complex_roots": ["(-p+sqrt(p^2-4q))/2", "(-p-sqrt(p^2-4q))/2"],
          "real_root_conditions": "Two distinct real roots when p^2-4q>0; one repeated real root -p/2 when p^2-4q=0; no real roots when p^2-4q<0.",
          "derived_quantity": "The sum of the squares of the two roots, with multiplicity, is p^2-2q.",
          "domain_exclusions": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "1053",
      "source_number": "1053",
      "text": "1053. а) 已知 $x_1$ 和 $x_2$ 是方程 $x^2-8x+k=0$ 的根，并且 $3x_1+4x_2=29$。求 $k$ 的值。б) 已知 $x_1$ 和 $x_2$ 是方程 $3x^2+2x+k=0$ 的根，并且$2x_1=-3x_2$。求 $k$ 的值。",
      "figure_refs": [],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1053a",
          "source_excerpt": "а) 已知 $x_1$ 和 $x_2$ 是方程 $x^2-8x+k=0$ 的根，并且 $3x_1+4x_2=29$。求 $k$ 的值。",
          "derivation": [
            "x1+x2=8. Subtract 3(x1+x2)=24 from 3x1+4x2=29 to get x2=5, then x1=3.",
            "k=x1*x2=15. The polynomial factors as (x-3)(x-5).",
            "The given labels are fixed by the linear condition: 3*3+4*5=29; no ordering of roots is assumed."
          ],
          "parameter_conditions": "The unique admissible k is 15.",
          "labeled_roots": {"x1": "3", "x2": "5"},
          "real_roots": ["3", "5"],
          "all_complex_roots": ["3", "5"],
          "domain_exclusions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1053b",
          "source_excerpt": "б) 已知 $x_1$ 和 $x_2$ 是方程 $3x^2+2x+k=0$ 的根，并且$2x_1=-3x_2$。求 $k$ 的值。",
          "derivation": [
            "x1+x2=-2/3 and x1=-(3/2)x2. Thus -(1/2)x2=-2/3, so x2=4/3 and x1=-2.",
            "x1*x2=k/3=-8/3, hence k=-8. The polynomial factors as (x+2)(3x-4).",
            "2*(-2)=-3*(4/3)=-4 verifies the labeled constraint."
          ],
          "parameter_conditions": "The unique admissible k is -8.",
          "labeled_roots": {"x1": "-2", "x2": "4/3"},
          "real_roots": ["-2", "4/3"],
          "all_complex_roots": ["-2", "4/3"],
          "domain_exclusions": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "1054",
      "source_number": "1054",
      "text": "1054. 利用引进辅助变量的方法解下列方程：а) $(x^2+6x)^2+5(x^2+6x)=24$；б) $(x^2-2x-5)^2-2(x^2-2x-5)=3$；в) $(x^2+3x-25)^2-2(x^2+3x-25)=-7$；г) $(y+2)^4-(y+2)^2=12$。",
      "figure_refs": [],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1054a",
          "source_excerpt": "а) $(x^2+6x)^2+5(x^2+6x)=24$",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=x^2+6x=(x+3)^2-9, so real t>=-9.",
            "t^2+5t-24=(t-3)(t+8)=0; t=3 or -8, both in range.",
            "t=3 gives (x+3)^2=12 and x=-3+/-2sqrt(3).",
            "t=-8 gives (x+3)^2=1 and x=-2,-4. These substitutions are reversible."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["-3+2sqrt(3)", "-3-2sqrt(3)", "-2", "-4"],
          "all_complex_roots": ["-3+2sqrt(3)", "-3-2sqrt(3)", "-2", "-4"],
          "domain_exclusions": [],
          "root_completeness": "The two auxiliary roots each lift to two distinct real roots, accounting for the quartic's four roots."
        },
        {
          "id": "1054b",
          "source_excerpt": "б) $(x^2-2x-5)^2-2(x^2-2x-5)=3$",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=x^2-2x-5=(x-1)^2-6, so real t>=-6.",
            "t^2-2t-3=(t-3)(t+1)=0; t=3 or -1, both in range.",
            "t=3 gives (x-1)^2=9 and x=4,-2.",
            "t=-1 gives (x-1)^2=5 and x=1+/-sqrt(5)."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["4", "-2", "1+sqrt(5)", "1-sqrt(5)"],
          "all_complex_roots": ["4", "-2", "1+sqrt(5)", "1-sqrt(5)"],
          "domain_exclusions": [],
          "root_completeness": "Both auxiliary branches are included and all four quartic roots are real."
        },
        {
          "id": "1054c",
          "source_excerpt": "в) $(x^2+3x-25)^2-2(x^2+3x-25)=-7$",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=x^2+3x-25. The equation becomes t^2-2t+7=(t-1)^2+6=0.",
            "For real x, t is real and the left side is at least 6, so there is no real root. Equivalently, the original left side t^2-2t is at least -1 and cannot be -7.",
            "Over C, t=1+/-i*sqrt(6). Then x^2+3x-(26+/-i*sqrt(6))=0.",
            "The two discriminants are 113+/-4i*sqrt(6), neither zero."
          ],
          "real_roots": [],
          "all_complex_roots": [
            "(-3+sqrt(113+4i*sqrt(6)))/2",
            "(-3-sqrt(113+4i*sqrt(6)))/2",
            "(-3+sqrt(113-4i*sqrt(6)))/2",
            "(-3-sqrt(113-4i*sqrt(6)))/2"
          ],
          "domain_exclusions": [],
          "root_completeness": "Both nonreal auxiliary roots each lift to two roots; a real x cannot occur in either branch."
        },
        {
          "id": "1054d",
          "source_excerpt": "г) $(y+2)^4-(y+2)^2=12$",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=(y+2)^2, with real t>=0.",
            "t^2-t-12=(t-4)(t+3)=0.",
            "t=4 gives y+2=+/-2 and y=0,-4.",
            "t=-3 is excluded for real y; over C it gives y=-2+/-i*sqrt(3)."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["0", "-4"],
          "all_complex_roots": ["0", "-4", "-2+i*sqrt(3)", "-2-i*sqrt(3)"],
          "domain_exclusions": ["The auxiliary branch t=-3 is impossible over R, not over C."]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "1055",
      "source_number": "1055",
      "text": "1055. 解下列方程（两个互为倒数的分式中，一个用 $t$ 表示，另一个用 $\\frac{1}{t}$ 表示）：а) $\\frac{x^2-1}{x+7}+\\frac{x+7}{x^2-1}=2.5$；б) $\\frac{x^2-3x}{x-2}+\\frac{x-2}{x^2-3x}=2.5$；в) $\\frac{(y+1)^2}{3y-2}-\\frac{3y-2}{(y+1)^2}=3\\frac{3}{4}$。",
      "figure_refs": [],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1055a",
          "source_excerpt": "а) $\\frac{x^2-1}{x+7}+\\frac{x+7}{x^2-1}=2.5$",
          "domain": "x is real, x!=-7,-1,1. Both original denominators must be nonzero; numerator zeros of the first fraction are also forbidden because it is reciprocated.",
          "derivation": [
            "Set t=(x^2-1)/(x+7); t exists and is nonzero on the original domain.",
            "t+1/t=5/2 gives 2t^2-5t+2=(2t-1)(t-2)=0, so t=2 or 1/2.",
            "t=2 gives x^2-2x-15=(x-5)(x+3)=0, hence x=5,-3.",
            "t=1/2 gives 2x^2-x-9=0, hence x=(1+/-sqrt(73))/4.",
            "At excluded x=-7,-1,1 the t=2 polynomial values are 48,-12,-16 and the t=1/2 polynomial values are 96,-6,-8 respectively; no candidate is excluded.",
            "Each branch reversibly reconstructs the same nonzero t and hence satisfies the original reciprocal equation."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["5", "-3", "(1+sqrt(73))/4", "(1-sqrt(73))/4"],
          "all_complex_roots_on_original_domain": ["5", "-3", "(1+sqrt(73))/4", "(1-sqrt(73))/4"],
          "domain_exclusions": ["x=-7: first denominator zero", "x=-1 or x=1: first numerator and reciprocal denominator zero", "t=0: reciprocal undefined"],
          "root_completeness": "Every original-domain solution has t in {2,1/2}; both reconstructed quadratics have all their roots listed."
        },
        {
          "id": "1055b",
          "source_excerpt": "б) $\\frac{x^2-3x}{x-2}+\\frac{x-2}{x^2-3x}=2.5$",
          "domain": "x is real, x!=2,0,3. The numerator x(x-3) of the first fraction must be nonzero as well as x-2.",
          "derivation": [
            "Set t=(x^2-3x)/(x-2), t!=0. Again 2t^2-5t+2=0, so t=2 or 1/2.",
            "t=2 gives x^2-5x+4=(x-1)(x-4)=0, hence x=1,4.",
            "t=1/2 gives 2x^2-7x+2=0, hence x=(7+/-sqrt(33))/4.",
            "At excluded x=2,0,3 the first quadratic has values -2,4,-2 and the second has values -4,2,-1; none of the roots is forbidden.",
            "Nonzero t and the original denominators are restored in both branches; multiplying by t or x-2 has introduced no accepted excluded root."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["1", "4", "(7+sqrt(33))/4", "(7-sqrt(33))/4"],
          "all_complex_roots_on_original_domain": ["1", "4", "(7+sqrt(33))/4", "(7-sqrt(33))/4"],
          "domain_exclusions": ["x=2: first denominator zero", "x=0 or x=3: first numerator and reciprocal denominator zero", "t=0: reciprocal undefined"],
          "root_completeness": "Both possible nonzero auxiliary values and both roots of each reconstructed quadratic are included."
        },
        {
          "id": "1055c",
          "source_excerpt": "в) $\\frac{(y+1)^2}{3y-2}-\\frac{3y-2}{(y+1)^2}=3\\frac{3}{4}$",
          "domain": "y is real, y!=2/3,-1. The mixed number on the right is 15/4.",
          "derivation": [
            "Set t=(y+1)^2/(3y-2), t!=0. Then t-1/t=15/4.",
            "4t^2-15t-4=(4t+1)(t-4)=0, so t=4 or -1/4.",
            "t=4 gives y^2-10y+9=(y-1)(y-9)=0, hence y=1,9.",
            "t=-1/4 gives 4(y+1)^2+3y-2=4y^2+11y+2=0, hence y=(-11+/-sqrt(89))/8.",
            "At excluded y=2/3,-1 the first quadratic has values 25/9,20 and the second has values 100/9,-5, all nonzero.",
            "Both negative-t candidates have y<2/3 and y!=-1, consistent with a positive square numerator and negative denominator; no sign restriction is dropped."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["1", "9", "(-11+sqrt(89))/8", "(-11-sqrt(89))/8"],
          "all_complex_roots_on_original_domain": ["1", "9", "(-11+sqrt(89))/8", "(-11-sqrt(89))/8"],
          "domain_exclusions": ["y=2/3: first denominator zero", "y=-1: first numerator and reciprocal denominator zero", "t=0: reciprocal undefined"],
          "root_completeness": "All roots from both admissible auxiliary values are real and within the original rational domain."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "1056",
      "source_number": "1056",
      "text": "1056. 指出经过怎样的变换方能把已知方程化成关于新变量的二次方程，再利用这种方法解方程：а) $(2x^2+7x-8)(2x^2+7x-3)-6=0$；б) $(x^2-10x-2)-2x^2+20x=15$。",
      "figure_refs": [],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1056a",
          "source_excerpt": "а) $(2x^2+7x-8)(2x^2+7x-3)-6=0$",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=2x^2+7x-8. The second factor is t+5, so t(t+5)-6=(t-1)(t+6)=0.",
            "Thus t=1 or -6. The real range is t>=-113/8, so both values are attainable.",
            "t=1 gives 2x^2+7x-9=(x-1)(2x+9)=0, hence x=1,-9/2.",
            "t=-6 gives 2x^2+7x-2=0, hence x=(-7+/-sqrt(65))/4.",
            "Both substitutions are equivalent to the original product equation."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["1", "-9/2", "(-7+sqrt(65))/4", "(-7-sqrt(65))/4"],
          "all_complex_roots": ["1", "-9/2", "(-7+sqrt(65))/4", "(-7-sqrt(65))/4"],
          "domain_exclusions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1056b",
          "source_excerpt": "б) $(x^2-10x-2)-2x^2+20x=15$",
          "exact_unsquared_equation": "$(x^2-10x-2)-2x^2+20x=15$",
          "derivation": [
            "Use the exact printed left side, with no exponent on the parenthesis: x^2-10x-2-2x^2+20x=-x^2+10x-2.",
            "The original equation is equivalent to x^2-10x+17=0, or (x-5)^2=8.",
            "A shift u=x-5 gives the quadratic u^2-8=0; u=+/-2sqrt(2), hence x=5+/-2sqrt(2).",
            "For comparison of instruction shape only, the natural t=x^2-10x-2 gives -2x^2+20x=-2(t+2); thus t-2(t+2)=15 is linear, t=-19. Reconstructing t=-19 again gives x^2-10x+17=0.",
            "At either literal root, x^2-10x=-17, so the printed left side is -(-17)-2=15."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["5+2sqrt(2)", "5-2sqrt(2)"],
          "all_complex_roots": ["5+2sqrt(2)", "5-2sqrt(2)"],
          "domain_exclusions": [],
          "preserved_risk": "1056b-unsquared-instruction-shape",
          "root_completeness": "The literal polynomial is quadratic with discriminant 32, not quartic; its two roots are complete."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "1057",
      "source_number": "1057",
      "text": "1057. 解下列双二次方程，并求根的和与积：а) $x^4-15x^2+50=0$； б) $x^4-x^2-12=0$；в) $36y^4-13y^2+1=0$； г) $16y^4+15y^2-1=0$。",
      "figure_refs": [],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1057a",
          "source_excerpt": "а) $x^4-15x^2+50=0$",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=x^2>=0 over R. t^2-15t+50=(t-5)(t-10)=0.",
            "Both auxiliary values are positive, giving x=+/-sqrt(5),+/-sqrt(10).",
            "Real-root sum is 0 and product is (-5)(-10)=50. All four roots are real, so the all-complex sum/product agree."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["sqrt(5)", "-sqrt(5)", "sqrt(10)", "-sqrt(10)"],
          "real_root_sum": "0",
          "real_root_product": "50",
          "all_complex_roots": ["sqrt(5)", "-sqrt(5)", "sqrt(10)", "-sqrt(10)"],
          "all_complex_root_sum_with_multiplicity": "0",
          "all_complex_root_product_with_multiplicity": "50",
          "domain_exclusions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1057b",
          "source_excerpt": "б) $x^4-x^2-12=0$",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=x^2>=0 over R. t^2-t-12=(t-4)(t+3)=0.",
            "Only t=4 is allowed over R, giving x=+/-2; their sum is 0 and product is -4.",
            "Over C, t=-3 additionally gives x=+/-i*sqrt(3). The four-root sum is 0 and product is (-4)*3=-12.",
            "The quartic Vieta product -12 is the all-complex product, not the product of the two real roots."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["2", "-2"],
          "real_root_sum": "0",
          "real_root_product": "-4",
          "all_complex_roots": ["2", "-2", "i*sqrt(3)", "-i*sqrt(3)"],
          "all_complex_root_sum_with_multiplicity": "0",
          "all_complex_root_product_with_multiplicity": "-12",
          "domain_exclusions": ["t=-3 is excluded only from the real-root inventory."]
        },
        {
          "id": "1057c",
          "source_excerpt": "в) $36y^4-13y^2+1=0$",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=y^2>=0 over R. 36t^2-13t+1=(4t-1)(9t-1)=0.",
            "t=1/4,1/9 give y=+/-1/2,+/-1/3.",
            "The four real roots sum to 0 and have product (-1/4)(-1/9)=1/36. The all-complex inventory is the same."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["1/2", "-1/2", "1/3", "-1/3"],
          "real_root_sum": "0",
          "real_root_product": "1/36",
          "all_complex_roots": ["1/2", "-1/2", "1/3", "-1/3"],
          "all_complex_root_sum_with_multiplicity": "0",
          "all_complex_root_product_with_multiplicity": "1/36",
          "domain_exclusions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1057d",
          "source_excerpt": "г) $16y^4+15y^2-1=0$",
          "derivation": [
            "Let t=y^2>=0 over R. 16t^2+15t-1=(16t-1)(t+1)=0.",
            "t=1/16 gives the two real roots y=+/-1/4; t=-1 is excluded over R.",
            "The two real roots sum to 0 and have product -1/16.",
            "Over C, t=-1 also gives y=+/-i. All four roots sum to 0 and have product (-1/16)*1=-1/16.",
            "The two products happen to agree numerically, but the real and all-complex root inventories are different."
          ],
          "real_roots": ["1/4", "-1/4"],
          "real_root_sum": "0",
          "real_root_product": "-1/16",
          "all_complex_roots": ["1/4", "-1/4", "i", "-i"],
          "all_complex_root_sum_with_multiplicity": "0",
          "all_complex_root_product_with_multiplicity": "-1/16",
          "domain_exclusions": ["t=-1 is excluded only from the real-root inventory."]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "1058",
      "source_number": "1058",
      "text": "1058. 证明：а) $\\sqrt{3+\\sqrt{7}}$ 是双二次方程 $x^4-6x^2+2=0$ 的根；б) $\\sqrt{\\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}}$ 是双二次方程 $x^4-3x^2+1=0$ 的根。",
      "figure_refs": [],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1058a",
          "source_excerpt": "а) $\\sqrt{3+\\sqrt{7}}$ 是双二次方程 $x^4-6x^2+2=0$ 的根",
          "domain": "The stated square root is the positive real principal root.",
          "derivation": [
            "For r=sqrt(3+sqrt(7)), r^2=3+sqrt(7) and r^4=16+6sqrt(7).",
            "r^4-6r^2+2=16+6sqrt(7)-18-6sqrt(7)+2=0, proving the exact requested claim.",
            "For completeness, t=x^2 solves t^2-6t+2=0, so t=3+/-sqrt(7). Both are positive because 9>7.",
            "Both signs of each square root give the full root inventory."
          ],
          "proved_root": "sqrt(3+sqrt(7))",
          "real_roots": ["sqrt(3+sqrt(7))", "-sqrt(3+sqrt(7))", "sqrt(3-sqrt(7))", "-sqrt(3-sqrt(7))"],
          "all_complex_roots": ["sqrt(3+sqrt(7))", "-sqrt(3+sqrt(7))", "sqrt(3-sqrt(7))", "-sqrt(3-sqrt(7))"],
          "domain_exclusions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1058b",
          "source_excerpt": "б) $\\sqrt{\\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}}$ 是双二次方程 $x^4-3x^2+1=0$ 的根",
          "domain": "The stated square root is the positive real principal root.",
          "derivation": [
            "For r=sqrt((3+sqrt(5))/2), r^2=(3+sqrt(5))/2 and r^4=(7+3sqrt(5))/2.",
            "r^4-3r^2+1=(7+3sqrt(5)-9-3sqrt(5)+2)/2=0.",
            "For completeness, t=x^2 solves t^2-3t+1=0, so t=(3+/-sqrt(5))/2.",
